          %h2#overview Overview
          %p
            In his influential 1821 textbook
            = succeed "," do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cours+d%27Analyse"} Cours d'Analyse
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Augustin+Cauchy"} Augustin Cauchy
            states a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/theorem"} theorem
            that is now widely regarded as
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/false"} false
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pointwise+convergence"} pointwise convergence
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/uniform+convergence"} uniform convergence
          %p
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/counterexample"} Counterexamples
            (specific
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Fourier+series"} Fourier series
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Joseph+Fourier"} Joseph Fourier
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Niels+Abel"} Niels Abel
            specifically pointed them out as counterexamples to Cauchy's claim. However, Cauchy denied that these were
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/counterexamples"} counterexamples
            %span.newWikiWord
              Imre Lakatos
              %a{:href => "/nlab/new/Imre+Lakatos"} ?
            has argued that the confusion rests on different conceptions of the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuum"} continuum
          %p
            Although Cauchy's original formulation was about the sum of an
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinite+series"} infinite series
            = succeed ";" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinite+sequence"} infinite sequence
